root causes fixed:
1. tryImplFunctionType types loop had no handler for 'R' (pseudogeneric layout-req sig start).
   Added tryParsePseudogenericSig() method: parses (Rl<subj>C)+ r<N>_l pattern.
   Also handles bare 'l' after pseudogeneric sig as @substituted 1-param inner sig marker.

2. implFnAttrsModeStart (and buildImplFnDisplay) did not skip 'P' (pseudogeneric marker).
   Added 'P' skip after 's' skip in both functions.

3. buildImplFnDisplay had wrong ordering: @substituted came before funcConv/coroAttr.
   Fixed order: calleeConv → funcConv → coroAttr → pseudoSigStr → @substituted.

4. buildImplFnDisplay had no 'Y<conv>' yield result handling.
   Added Y<conv> loop between params and regular results (renders as "@yields <conv> <type>").

5. implFnTypesNeeded had no 'Y<conv>' counting.
   Added Y<conv> loop so type count is correct for attrs like "sPetWAlYl".

6. After types loop, if implSigStr empty but innerSubstitutedParamCount > 0, build sigStr.
   Also if implSubsStr empty but pendingForClause non-empty, use as implSubsStr.
   This handles the outer @substituted impl-fn case with pseudogeneric sig.

